# Snap apps for graphical Linux machines (display = true).
# Installed by run_after_18-linux-desktop-snaps.sh (stamp-and-compare).
#
# ONLY apps whose official/best Linux channel is the Snap Store belong here —
# everything else is a Brewfile `flatpak` (Flathub), a vendor apt repo
# (packages.apt), or a GitHub .deb installer. Keep this list minimal.
#   raindrop        -> Raindrop.io (official snap; no maintained Flathub app)
#   signal-desktop  -> Signal (official snap; apt repo only covers Debian/Ubuntu)
#   todoist         -> Todoist (official snap by Doist; no official Flathub app)
#
# The installer skips any package already installed via dpkg on apt-based
# distros (e.g. signal-desktop from the Signal apt repo on Ubuntu/Debian),
# so apt-based and RPM-based machines converge on the same packages.snap file.
#
# Names only, one per line — the installer extracts via `grep -Ev '^#|^$'`.
raindrop
signal-desktop
todoist
